1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,657
Hi Francesco, Nissan here. Good to hear from you after Bali.

2
00:00:03,707 --> 00:00:08,846
You said our fields are close, so I put Awareland into our sandbox to see how close.

3
00:00:09,498 --> 00:00:15,465
Reddi Agent Protocol is a marketplace on Solana where agents pay for AI services from a Budget.

4
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:21,608
You lock money once, give your agent a key, and every call it pays for comes back with a receipt.

5
00:00:22,261 --> 00:00:26,004
The key already has limits on chain. It can reserve and close.

6
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:29,736
It can't withdraw, and it can't pay anyone who hasn't joined.

7
00:00:29,786 --> 00:00:36,282
What it can't tell you is who is behind the agent, or whether the job matches what its owner signed off on.

8
00:00:36,332 --> 00:00:37,934
That's your side of things.

9
00:00:38,595 --> 00:00:45,430
So in the sandbox, before the agent reserves a cent, it asks Awareland two questions. Who runs this agent?

10
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:51,859
And does the key match the mandate: five dollars at most, seventy-two hours, joined providers only?

11
00:00:51,909 --> 00:00:53,158
Awareland says pass.

12
00:00:53,814 --> 00:00:55,960
Then the agent gets on with the job.

13
00:00:56,010 --> 00:01:02,852
Tolca checks each provider's payout wallet first, and every call lands on a receipt chained to the one before it.

14
00:01:03,503 --> 00:01:06,837
The Budget closes and a 24-hour dispute window runs.

15
00:01:06,887 --> 00:01:12,498
Each provider is paid what its receipts add up to, and the rest goes back to the buyer.

16
00:01:13,149 --> 00:01:19,151
In the demo the Awareland check is simulated, and free, because I didn't want to guess your price.

17
00:01:19,201 --> 00:01:26,129
I'd love to make it real: a paid check any agent can run from its Budget, or the trust layer behind our registry.

18
00:01:26,179 --> 00:01:29,526
Good luck closing the raise. Let's find a time to talk.
